body:
I'm seeing this same issue, this time with an image, and have a simple reproduction.  I'm on bevy 0.9, and macos 12.6, m1 max cpu.

What I'm trying to do is clip off half of an image.  The parent node is half the height of the child, and has overflow set to hidden.

You'll notice that the image is heavily distorted.  Setting overflow to visible fixes the warping, as does changing the container height to be the same as the child image height.

I have a simple reproduction here:
```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new().add_plugins(DefaultPlugins).add_startup_system(setup).run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands, asset_server: Res<AssetServer>) {
    const IMG_SIZE: f32 = 256.0;
    const CONTAINER_HEIGHT: f32 = 128.0;
    
    // ui camera
    commands.spawn(Camera2dBundle::default());
    commands
        .spawn(NodeBundle {
            style: Style {
                size: Size::new(Val::Px(IMG_SIZE), Val::Px(CONTAINER_HEIGHT)),
                overflow: Overflow::Hidden,
                ..default()
            },
            background_color: Color::RED.into(),
            ..default()
        })
        .with_children(|parent| {
            parent.spawn(ImageBundle {
                style: Style {
                    size: Size::new(Val::Px(IMG_SIZE), Val::Px(IMG_SIZE)),
                    ..default()
                },
                image: UiImage(asset_server.load("pause.png")),
                ..default()
            });
        });
}
```
Here's the `pause.png` image:
![pause](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5114062/210926886-5d941e18-f762-45e5-8c33-e4ea66a0cfa0.png)

Here's a screenshot of what bevy is rendering:
<img width="292" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5114062/210927066-5d97ce8f-06ab-450a-8ba2-471ef6ea5ae2.png">

Here's what it looks like with `Overflow::Visible`:
<img width="278" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5114062/210928726-f32efed5-d25d-4485-956e-5a2ee94582b8.png">

I can reproduce this on bevy main as well. The issue seems scale-factor dependent. It isn't present with
```rust
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins.set(WindowPlugin {
            window: WindowDescriptor {
                scale_factor_override: Some(1.),
                ..default()
            },
            ..default()
        }))
```
